  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25d-perchlike-fishes-4-south-american-dwarf-cichlids/apistogramma_gephyra_en/",
      "html": "<p>A pretty blackwater Apistogramma that is imported only very occasionally. It looks quite similar to A. agassizii and its aquarium maintenance is comparable to that well-known species. Available size: 3-5 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25d-perchlike-fishes-4-south-american-dwarf-cichlids/apistogramma_gephyra_en/",
      "html": "<p>The fish originates from Brazil, where it is found in the central Rio Negro and lower Rio Branco basins.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25d-perchlike-fishes-4-south-american-dwarf-cichlids/apistogramma_gephyra_en/",
      "html": "<p>The yellow face mask of the male is very obvious in the population currently available. Females stay much smaller than the males, as usual in Apistogramma.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25d-perchlike-fishes-4-south-american-dwarf-cichlids/apistogramma_gephyra_en/",
      "html": "<p>Apistogramma: ancient Greek, meaning \"with unreliable line\". It is not known whether the lateral line organ or the pattern is meant. gephyra: after the ancient Greek word for \"bridge\", which refers to the intermediate position of the species between Apistogramma agassizii and A. pertensis.</p>"
    }
  ],
